<title>USA: Sinclair to sell Oklahoma TV station.</title>
<headline>Sinclair to sell Oklahoma TV station.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sinclair Broadcast Group Inc said Wednesday it signed a letter of intent to sell the assets of KOKH-TV, Oklahoma City, to Sullivan Broadcasting for $60 million in cash.</p>
<p>KOKH-TV is currently owned by Heritage Media Corp, and Sinclair said it is required to divest KOKH-TV pursuant to the terms of its agreement to buy the television and radio stations of Heritage.</p>
<p>Sinclair said its acquisition of Heritage's television and radio stations is contingent on News Corp Ltd's acquisition of Heritage Media.</p>
<p>Each of these transactions is subject to Federal Communications Commission and Justice Department approval.</p>
<p>Sullivan is a privately-held company.</p>
</text>
